  - mechanistic interpretability
  - transformers
  - MuJoCo
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered mechanistic study of small transformers trained from scratch to adapt in-context to unknown
  dynamics: linear systems with unknown parameters, one-degree-of-freedom MuJoCo systems with contact, and linear
  adaptive control. The predictors are Bayes-optimal while data are scarce, then settle at an approximation floor;
  the pre-registered residual-stream mechanism is rejected; exploratory analyses with dimension-matched controls
  localise the sufficient statistics of the context in the attention key-value memory of the last two blocks.
  The pre-registration is the commit tagged prereg-d134c5a.
